// Expected: e0 at one session and e1 at two.
//
// Bob decrypts under a check and forwards the plaintext to Carol under a
// guard; Carol hashes what she is handed. Replacing the nonce on the way to
// Bob makes his checked decryption fail, and a principal that halts at a
// check sends nothing after it: Carol never receives d and never computes x.
// A comparison between Alice's hash and a value Carol never reached is not
// a divergence, so at one session the query holds.
//
// The engine used to compare it anyway: the halt withheld Bob's own slots,
// but Carol's x, computed from a slot she was never handed, was read as
// reached, and it resolved to a hash of the failed decryption. A slot whose
// definition reads a withheld slot is now withheld too. At two sessions the
// attacker routes the other session's nonce and ciphertext into Bob, who
// decrypts m#2 under the shared key and hands it on, and Carol's hash of it
// genuinely differs from Alice's.

attacker[active]

principal Alice[
	knows private k
	generates m, n
	e = AEAD_ENC(k, n, m, nil)
	hm = HASH(m)
]

Alice -> Bob: n, e

principal Bob[
	knows private k
	d = AEAD_DEC(k, n, e, nil)?
]

Bob -> Carol: [d]

principal Carol[
	x = HASH(d)
]

queries[
	equivalence? hm, x
]
